iform falling water or white noise.\n2.  Evaluate Option A (waterfall): A waterfall is a loud, continuous water sound, similar to heavy rain.\n3.  Evaluate Option B (static noise): Static noise is a form of white noise, which shares acoustic properties with the sound of rain hitting surfaces.\n4.  Evaluate Option D (shower running): A shower produces falling water sounds, very similar to rain.\n5.  Evaluate Option C (car engine starting): This is a distinct mechanical sound involving combustion and moving parts, which does not resemble the sound of falling water or general white noise associated with rain. Therefore, it is the sound least likely to be mistaken for rain.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{C}$
