ity of the neck, the second speaker's sarcasm is about the *treatment* (massage), not the ailment itself.\n    *   D) enjoys being sarcastic with friends: While they are being sarcastic, the *reason* the comment is sarcastic relates to the content (the massage suggestion), not just a general enjoyment of sarcasm.\n\nThe sarcasm hinges on the speaker saying they "relish" something they clearly dislike, which is the idea of a stranger touching them intimately (massage).\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{B}$
