ing, implying he *doesn't* want that official status, making B a better explanation for the *sarcasm* itself.\n\nThe sarcasm is used to express an unwillingness or discomfort with formalizing or defining the situation, which points to reluctance to define the relationship.\n\nReasoning: The man sarcastically states he does not want to put a label on the situation involving his ex-wife and her friend. This sarcastic denial strongly suggests an underlying reluctance or discomfort with formally defining or categorizing that relationship dynamic.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{B}$
