ental music is always longer in duration than classical pieces.** This is factually incorrect. Both genres contain pieces of varying lengths.\n\n3.  **Conclusion:** Choice A provides the most accurate and fundamental contrast between the general characteristics of experimental music (which the audio suggests) and traditional classical music regarding structure and rules. The music heard is structurally ambiguous, fitting the description of breaking traditional rules.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{A}$
